Sail: the picture-in-picture window behaves like Oblò.
- Dragging the video moves the window; it stops at the screen edges, the menu
  bar and the Dock, and crosses to another screen where they touch (as in Arc).
- It can be as large as the screen (Chromium stops at 80%).
- A click shows or hides the controls, a double click (or F) fills the screen.
- Keys: K play/pause, J/L back/forward 10 s, Up/Down volume, M mute,
  Esc back to the tab.
- The volume is the tab's media session volume; it goes back to 100% when the
  window closes, so the page's own volume control still counts.

Play in the window also starts the video itself, not only the site's play
action: a site in a hidden tab can ignore it, leaving the video paused.

